  <h2>Context</h2>
  <p>
    Galaxy's electronic trading business needed reliable, scalable, low-latency infrastructure. I joined as Vice President of Site Reliability Engineering in 2022 and later became Director, Principal SRE.
  </p>

  <h2>What I built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Kubernetes clusters as the standard runtime for trading and DeFi services, extending container and microservice architecture across the firm.</li>
    <li>Flux as the firm-wide GitOps standard, automating continuous delivery of applications and Kubernetes platform components in every environment.</li>
    <li>Infrastructure-as-code and CI/CD workflows that raised engineering productivity and release speed.</li>
    <li>The infrastructure, networking and reliability foundations for the RFS trading platform and the EMS/PMS execution and portfolio management systems.</li>
    <li>On-premises bare-metal infrastructure on Equinix Metal, extending the firm beyond the public cloud.</li>
    <li>Zscaler zero trust (ZIA and ZPA) for internet access and private application access across the firm.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Beyond trading</h2>
  <p>
    For six months I also led Corporate Network and Systems Engineering, overseeing the firm's corporate network and enterprise systems. Throughout, I pushed DevOps and SRE practice across engineering teams to make electronic trading systems more reliable and easier to operate.
  </p>
